Subject: [PATCH] 3270: a company typed in its English spelling reaches its
 Georgian label
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

ME-037, 2 of 2: „ვინ მყავს Colliers-ში?" missed the contact saved as
„ნიკა კოლიერსი". normalize_search_token gives „colliers" and „koliersi"
(trigram similarity 0.2), and the Georgian readings of a Latin word were
made letter by letter (c → ც), so no term reached the label.

buildSearchTerms now also reads an English spelling as it sounds before
making its Georgian readings: a hard c (and ck) is k, a doubled consonant is
one. „Colliers" → „koliers" → „კოლიერს", which the label contains. Words
that sound as spelled add nothing. Server search only, no new words.

Not covered here: the second half of ME-037 („რა იცი ნიკა კოლიერსზე?"
answered „saved as a friend"), which is how the model reads the label.

